1:cmd:group attributes origin igp next-hop 101.1.101.1 local-preference 100 community [100:1] extended-community [target:65001:1] ; withdraw route 1.4.0.0/16 rd 65000:1 label 1000
1:raw:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:004B:02:00000034800F11000180688000000000FDE80000000101044001010040020040050400000064C0080400640001C010080002FDE900000001
# The raw frame above carries 800000 where upstream ExaBGP sends 003E81, the
# label the command names. RFC 8277 Section 2.4 names those three octets in an
# MP_UNREACH_NLRI the Compatibility field and says "Upon transmission, the
# Compatibility field SHOULD be set to 0x800000.", so Ze writes that value on
# every withdrawal it sends, whatever the command says.
# The withdraw document carries no `label`, where upstream's carries [[1000,16001]].
# The same section says "Upon reception, the value of the Compatibility field
# MUST be ignored." Ze decodes a withdrawal that way, so the field never reaches a
# script as a label (docs/exabgp/exabgp-differences.md, "Withdrawal labels").
1:json:{"exabgp":"6.0.0","type":"update","neighbor":{"address":{"local":"127.0.0.1","peer":"127.0.0.1"},"asn":{"local":1,"peer":1},"router-id":"1.2.3.4","direction":"in","message":{"update":{"attribute":{"origin":"igp","local-preference":100,"community":[[100,1]],"extended-community":[{"value":842127122628609,"string":"target:65001:1"}]},"withdraw":{"ipv4 mpls-vpn":[{"nlri":"1.4.0.0/16","rd":"65000:1"}]}}}}}

